# Contributor tools

This directory contains build, content-production, evaluation, and release helpers.
Start with the [tool guide](../docs/tools/README.md) or the relevant topic in the
[documentation index](../docs/README.md). Run commands from the repository root
unless a tool's guide says otherwise.

## Common workflows

- `dev_build.py`: routine development builds; see [development](../docs/development/README.md).
- `check_docs.py`: Markdown links and navigation; see [documentation maintenance](../docs/development/documentation.md).
- `tournaments/`: local and SSH evaluation; see [distributed tournaments](../docs/tools/tournaments.md).
- `artwork/` and `unit-animation/`: reviewed asset inputs and rendering; see [assets](../docs/assets/README.md).
- `music/`: soundtrack production and validation; see [music pipeline](../docs/assets/music-pipeline.md).
- `world_atlas.py`: geography inputs for the Continents generator; see [world atlas](../docs/map-generators/world-atlas.md).
- `release/`: package helpers; see [releases](../docs/releases/README.md).

## Legacy sprite utility

`mksprite.cpp` packs images into sprite sheets. Its explicit `scons mksprite` target
uses `Magick++-config` from an installed ImageMagick development environment, as
declared in `tools/SConscript`. Current artwork workflows are documented under
[assets](../docs/assets/README.md).

This extensionless README is retained because source-distribution packaging names
it explicitly. Contributor dependencies are pinned in `requirements-dev.txt`;
individual workflows document isolated or hardware-specific environments.
